      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Felton%2C_California"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s historic Covered Bridge, built in 1892, spans the San Lorenzo River and sits on the National Register of Historic Places.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Felton%2C_California"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Felton’s railroad history includes the 1875 Santa Cruz and Felton Railroad terminus and the 1963 Roaring Camp tourist line starting at the Old Felton Depot.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10,
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Felton%2C_California"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The first redwood preserve in the United States began in Felton when a 1867 logging purchase was turned into a protected forest.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://californiawanderland.com/felton/"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Felton’s Creamer Hotel (1875) and Alcazar Hall (1891) survived multiple fires, preserving a glimpse of the town’s 19th‑century architecture.",
